item.text:
I searched official Egyptian parliamentary, presidential/SIS, gazette, NCHR, and Arabic press materials. The strongest recoveries are the precise Article 53 successor framework and its presidential application in Sinai, including two 2022 renewals; Sisi’s direct operational instruction after the May attack; limited NCHR prison-monitoring evidence; and additional rhetoric that reinforces hostile labeling but still does not show incitement.

Still unresolved: no official investigation or discipline record concerning the execution videos; no published pardon-beneficiary annex; no underlying Hadhoud autopsy or complete case file; no independently accessible, year-specific prison-complaint results; and no recoverable 2021–2022 V-Dem physical-integrity rows. The V-Dem/OWID dataset page exposed its CSV endpoint but not Egypt’s rows through the accessible interface. Searches of additional 2022 speeches found repeated delegitimizing rhetoric, not a direction to attack the Brotherhood or other civilians.

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"House approves government bill amending the Anti-Terrorism Law","publisher":"Egyptian House of Representatives","publication_date":"2021-10-31","url":"https://www.parliament.gov.eg/News_Show.aspx?frm=4182","claim":"The government-sponsored amendment to Article 53 of Anti-Terrorism Law No. 94/2015 required a presidential decree imposing counterterrorism measures in specified areas to identify the authority empowered to issue implementing decisions. The House recorded prior consultation with the Supreme Police Council, National Defence Council, and Supreme Judicial Council. Together with the enacted text summarized by Egypt's NCHR, the framework authorized the president, for renewable periods of up to six months, to order evacuation, isolation, curfew, and related measures when terrorist danger existed.","locator":"House article lines 35-49, especially 47-49; NCHR report PDF pp. 12-13, lines 474-484, identifying Law No. 149/2021 and the six-month Article 53 powers","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C2-001","canonical_fact_key":"egypt_anti_terrorism_law_149_2021_article_53_successor_emergency_framework","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.5"],"source_type":"official_legislative_record","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official parliamentary record identifies the bill, institutional consultations, provision amended, and implementing-authority requirement; the later NCHR report supplies a stable enacted-law summary, although the gazette text itself was not retrievable.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The law was enacted immediately before 2022 and remained the legal basis for presidential Sinai measures applied throughout 2022.","ruler_attribution":"The provision expressly assigns the exceptional-measures decision to the president and requires his decree to designate the implementing authority.","contrary_evidence":"The measures require parliamentary presentation and are geographically and temporally specified, providing formal checks; the sources do not establish that every authorized measure was actually imposed everywhere.","underlying_fact_key":"sisi_2022_article53_sinai_exceptional_measures","lenses":["3B.5"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"House approves Presidential Decree No. 130/2022 imposing precautionary measures in Sinai for six months","publisher":"Egyptian House of Representatives","publication_date":"2022-03-30","url":"https://www.parliament.gov.eg/News_Show.aspx?frm=4379","claim":"The House approved Sisi's Decree No. 130/2022 extending Decree No. 442/2021 for six months from April 3, 2022. The presidential decree authorized some or all of a specified menu of measures in parts of Sinai: curfews, business-hour controls, evacuation, residence and access prohibitions, communications restrictions, restrictions on licensed firearms, motorcycles and four-wheel-drive vehicles, drones, and dual-use explosive materials. This is direct evidence that Sisi personally maintained the successor exceptional-power regime during the period.","locator":"Lines 35-48, especially line 47 for the six-month extension and line 48 for the enumerated measures","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C2-002","canonical_fact_key":"sisi_decree_130_2022_sinai_exceptional_measures","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.5","3B.2"],"source_type":"official_legislative_decision_record","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official House record gives the decree number, approval, effective date, duration, territorial scope, and enumerated powers.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The extension operated from April 3 into October 2022.","ruler_attribution":"The record identifies the measure as Sisi's presidential decree; implementation remained shared with the designated military and administrative authorities.","contrary_evidence":"The House approved the decree by majority, and the record frames it as a response to actual security conditions. Authorization of measures does not prove that each measure was used or abused in a particular locality.","underlying_fact_key":"sisi_2022_article53_sinai_exceptional_measures","lenses":["3B.5","3B.2"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Egypt’s parliament approves extending security measures in Sinai for six months","publisher":"Ahram Online","publication_date":"2022-10-01","url":"https://english.ahram.org.eg/NewsContent/1/64/477057/Egypt/Politics-/Egypt%EF%BF%BDs-parliament-approves-extending-security-mea.aspx","claim":"On October 1, 2022, the House unanimously approved a further six-month extension of the president's security-measures decree for parts of Sinai. The parliamentary speaker stated that the House supported Armed Forces steps under Sisi's leadership. This establishes continuation of the presidentially owned exceptional-measures framework through the end of 2022, although the opened report does not give the new decree number or reproduce its operative text.","locator":"Headline and lines 47-56 for date and unanimous extension; lines 61 and 70-75 for parliamentary attribution to the Armed Forces under Sisi and the stated security rationale","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C2-003","canonical_fact_key":"sisi_october_2022_sinai_security_measures_extension","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.5","3B.2"],"source_type":"strong_state_aligned_reporting_on_legislative_action","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Ahram reporting directly describes the parliamentary vote, but the underlying decree number and gazette text were not recovered.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"The vote occurred October 1, 2022 and continued the measures beyond the end of the calendar year.","ruler_attribution":"The measure was an extension of the president's decree, and the speaker expressly described Armed Forces action as occurring under Sisi's leadership.","contrary_evidence":"Parliament unanimously approved the extension, and reporting notes a genuine decline in terrorist attacks following military operations. It does not establish how individual restrictions were implemented.","underlying_fact_key":"sisi_2022_article53_sinai_exceptional_measures","lenses":["3B.5","3B.2"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Sisi orders law-enforcement bodies to continue purging North Sinai of Takfiri groups","publisher":"Egypt State Information Service","publication_date":"2022-05-08","url":"https://sis.gov.eg/en/media-center/news/sisi-orders-law-enforcement-bodies-to-keep-purging-n-sinai-of-takfiri-groups/","claim":"After the May 7 western-Sinai attack, Sisi chaired the Supreme Council of the Armed Forces and instructed law-enforcement bodies to continue operations against terrorist groups in North Sinai. He reviewed efforts to pursue fugitives in cooperation with Sinai residents. This establishes direct presidential ownership of the broad counterinsurgency policy and cooperation with local forces, but it neither identifies the units shown in the later execution videos nor authorizes unlawful killings.","locator":"Indexed article dated May 8, 2022; paragraphs beginning 'President Abdel Fattah El Sisi instructed Sunday' and 'Sisi also followed up on efforts under way'","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C2-004","canonical_fact_key":"sisi_may_2022_directive_north_sinai_operations_local_cooperation","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.2","3B.9"],"source_type":"official_executive_statement","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Official state account directly attributes the strategic instruction and meeting to Sisi; the page intermittently returned 502, but its indexed text was available. It supplies policy-level attribution, not incident-level command evidence.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly concerns Sinai operations in May 2022, shortly before the execution-video material appeared.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential instruction and oversight of the overall operation are established; command or knowledge of the recorded executions is not.","contrary_evidence":"The directive followed a deadly militant attack and was framed as pursuit of terrorist fugitives. No language directing mistreatment, execution, or collective punishment was located.","underlying_fact_key":"sisi_2022_sinai_operational_authority","lenses":["3B.2","3B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Together to Promote Human Rights","publisher":"Egyptian National Council for Human Rights","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://nchr.eg/Uploads/publication/en/16reporten%5E1698138637.pdf","claim":"The NCHR reports that its delegations visited newly established Interior Ministry reform and rehabilitation centres during 2022 to examine penal-institution development, infrastructure, equipment, practices, legal compliance, and issues previously raised through complaints. It reports fourteen visits and discussions with Interior Ministry personnel about inmate complaints. This is evidence of a domestic monitoring and complaint-follow-up mechanism, but the visits were coordinated with the Interior Ministry and the report does not publish facility-level complaint findings, remedial orders, or an independently selected inmate sample.","locator":"PDF pp. 47-49, lines 1832-1837 and 1852-1885, especially lines 1852-1858 and 1878-1885","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C2-005","canonical_fact_key":"egypt_nchr_2022_prison_monitoring_visits","disposition":"context","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.4"],"source_type":"national_human_rights_institution_report","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"A domestic institutional report gives year-specific activity and visit purposes, but provides limited facility-level results and describes cooperation with the agency being monitored.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"The report specifically distinguishes its 2022 visits from its 2021 activity.","ruler_attribution":"Contextual state-remedy evidence under Sisi's administration; the report does not attribute the visits or any resulting remedy to a personal presidential decision.","contrary_evidence":"The report describes modern facilities, inmate engagement, and complaint discussions as improvements. Its lack of published adverse findings, methodology, or concrete remedies limits its value as proof of effective independent oversight.","underlying_fact_key":"egypt_2022_detention_oversight_and_remedy","lenses":["3B.4"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Sisi: ‘People of evil’ have only abuse and doubt about state projects","publisher":"El Watan","publication_date":"2022-09-08","url":"https://www.elwatannews.com/news/details/6287713","claim":"At a Suez Canal Authority event, Sisi described unnamed critics and hostile media as 'people of evil' who sought to make ordinary Egyptians despair, weaken, and fear, and urged that their earlier comments be displayed publicly to discredit them. This broadens the May finding from Brotherhood-specific labeling to hostile labeling of critical media and online voices. The located remarks advocate rebuttal and exposure, not physical attack or punishment.","locator":"Lines 76-105, especially the direct quotations at lines 103-105","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C2-006","canonical_fact_key":"sisi_september_2022_people_of_evil_critical_media_labeling","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.3"],"source_type":"contemporaneous_local_reporting_with_direct_quotation","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Arabic report provides extended direct quotations and event context, though an official transcript was not recovered.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct presidential remarks delivered September 8, 2022.","ruler_attribution":"The words are directly attributed to Sisi speaking publicly at an official event.","contrary_evidence":"The prescription in the quoted passage is media rebuttal and comparison with past claims; it contains no instruction to harm, detain, or attack critics.","underlying_fact_key":"sisi_2022_hostile_collective_labeling_without_incitement","lenses":["3B.3"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Sisi on the Muslim Brotherhood: They do not know what a state means","publisher":"El Watan","publication_date":"2022-07-03","url":"https://www.elwatannews.com/news/details/6175141","claim":"In remarks to journalists and media figures, Sisi stated that the Muslim Brotherhood did not understand what a state was and characterized its principal skill as organizing elections, influencing people, and establishing associations for doubt and abuse. The remarks are direct presidential delegitimization of a political-religious group, but the located wording contains no call for listeners or security forces to commit violence against its members.","locator":"Lines 69-93, especially direct quotations at lines 90 and 93","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C2-007","canonical_fact_key":"sisi_july_2022_brotherhood_delegitimization","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.3"],"source_type":"contemporaneous_local_reporting_with_direct_quotation","source_confidence":"medium-high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Arabic reporting supplies the occasion and extended direct quotations; no official transcript was recovered.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct presidential remarks delivered July 3, 2022.","ruler_attribution":"The quoted statements are Sisi's own public remarks.","contrary_evidence":"Although derogatory and delegitimizing, the passage does not advocate violence, detention, or private retaliation.","underlying_fact_key":"sisi_2022_hostile_collective_labeling_without_incitement","lenses":["3B.3"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON:{"title":"Presidential Decree No. 155/2022 pardoning categories of convicts for Sinai Liberation Day and Eid al-Fitr","publisher":"Egyptian Government Printing Affairs Authority","publication_date":"2022-04-19","url":"https://alamiria.com/Sec/TashTxt?id=OBywabEeh1U%3D","claim":"Sisi issued Decree No. 155/2022 granting remission of the remaining custodial punishment to defined eligibility classes for Sinai Liberation Day and Eid al-Fitr after consulting the cabinet. The decree is another official 2022 instance of direct presidential ownership of a class-based pardon mechanism. Its opened/indexed text lists statutory predicates and begins the eligibility rules, but it does not publish a named beneficiary annex and therefore cannot verify that particular police officers received relief.","locator":"Official text heading and preamble through 'قرر'; Article 1 beginning with the first eligibility class for prisoners serving life sentences who had completed fifteen years by April 25, 2022","provisional_id":"WEB-3B-C2-008","canonical_fact_key":"sisi_decree_155_2022_class_based_pardon","disposition":"final_evidence","chapter_ids":["3B"],"methodology_ids":["3B.4"],"source_type":"official_gazette_legal_text","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government printing authority identifies the decree, issuing president, occasion, legal bases, cabinet consultation, and eligibility structure. It contains no recovered named-beneficiary annex.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Issued and operative in April 2022.","ruler_attribution":"The pardon decree was issued personally by President Sisi under his constitutional and statutory clemency authority.","contrary_evidence":"The decree supports a general clemency mechanism and may have benefited ordinary prisoners; without a beneficiary annex it neither proves nor disproves the reported pardon of officers convicted in custodial-death cases.","underlying_fact_key":"sisi_2022_class_based_presidential_pardons","lenses":["3B.4"]}
